    <string name="help_title">How to use</string>
    <string name="help_head_gesture">Gestures</string>
    <string name="help_body_gesture">Tap: squash and bounce, plus a random tap reaction\nDouble tap: panel (balance, local and account today/total, weather); cycles Look at weather / Check wallet\nTriple tap: your chosen app (none by default; a triple tap reminds you to pick one on Home)\nLong press: about 0.6 s and the menu appears at once (no need to release)\nDrag: move the pet; a hard fling flies off and bounces off the edges</string>
    <string name="help_head_idle">What she does by herself</string>
    <string name="help_body_idle">Idle: random everyday actions; 23:00–06:00 sleep actions.\nDaytime: a short move every 1.5–3 min — horizontal (fast, walking assets) / vertical (slow, floating assets) / diagonal (4 directions, assets by speed)</string>
    <string name="help_head_temp_hide">Hide for now</string>
    <string name="help_body_temp_hide">Hides the pet until you leave the current app. Needs Usage access or Accessibility; otherwise it will not return by itself — use Summon on Home.</string>
    <string name="help_head_auto_hide">Auto-hide</string>
    <string name="help_body_auto_hide">Hides while a game or full-screen video is in front, then returns. Requires Accessibility.</string>
    <string name="help_group_dsh">Only worth reading if you use DSH (skip otherwise)</string>
    <string name="help_group_dsh_body">Status sync: thinking / working / waiting for your confirmation / needs your answer / error / round finished each have their own action.\n\nCommand confirmation: when DSH asks, the pet shows Allow once / Deny; after 90 s without input it hands control back.\n\nQuestion reminders: when DSH needs a choice or answer, a persistent bubble plus a waiting action appear, cleared once you answer.\n\nAccount data: sign in once on the Data tab (phone, or email and password); the panel then shows balance, account today and total, and asks you to sign in again if the token expires.\n\nLocal spending: reads the local DSH usage ledger; DSH must be running with the data bridge plugin loaded.</string>
